 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "One unit: the reciter joins 142→147 (about 165 s). 143 (Allah speaking, «أرني أنظر إليك», «فلما تجلى ربه للجبل»): no motif, nothing literal, mountains mood only; Allah's answer «لن تراني» is not paraphrased (first person). Musa: no motif. An hourglass for the forty nights, a book for the tablets, two paths for «سبيل الرشد… سبيل الغي». 145:18-20 «دار الفاسقين» is not glossed (the tafsirs differ). First-person «سأصرف… آياتي» not paraphrased. STAGING v4: c1 (142-143) stays ambient (night_sky: no central light source) on purpose: 143 is Allah speaking to Musa, his request to see Him, and the manifestation to the mountain; one chapter, so 142 stays with it. Nothing is drawn for Musa, Harun, the mountain or its levelling; no light, glow, plate or camera move on 143:25-29: the camera holds wide from 143:22 to 143:30 (holds only), and params.quiet turns off the background's word pulses over all of 143:1-35 (Allah speaking, the request to see Him, the manifestation to the mountain), so nothing brightens with His speech or on 143:24-29. An hourglass for the forty nights (142:3-8), a two-paths plate for the way of reform and the way of the corrupters (142:19-23), a geometric plate for his glorification of Allah (143:36). c2 (144-145) also stays ambient (night_sky: the appointment is counted in nights; not light, as 145:18-20 can be a threat): it is Allah speaking to Musa alone and writing the tablets for him, with no one else present, and a mountain stage right after 143 would show an intact mountain behind Musa as Allah speaks; nothing is a voice source: params.quiet turns off the word pulses over all of 144-145; transition dissolve (no light sweep after 143). A scroll plate for take what I have given you (144:9-11) and a book plate for the tablets (145:4-11); 145:18-20 (the abode of the defiantly disobedient: Al-Muyassar the Fire, As-Sa'di their ruined homes) is not drawn. c3 (146-147): the arrogant deniers, three faceless men in dark robes in a town: the camera on them for their arrogance (146:5); a two-paths plate for the way of guidance and the way of error (146:19-29); they shake their heads on 146:32 (they denied) and turn away on 146:36 (heedless); a leaf plate for their deeds come to nothing (147:6). Nothing of the Hereafter is drawn."
 },
